# Directory patterns below are ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose.
# A bare `data/` matches at every level, not just the repo root -- it silently
# swallowed src/fitymi/data/, the package the whole codebase sits on, and the loss
# was invisible because the working tree still had the files. Anything that names a
# top-level artefact directory gets a leading slash.
/data/
/runs/
/outputs/
/results/
/wandb/
/.venv/
/venv/
.env

# These are meant to match at any depth.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store

# Model weights, wherever they land.
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.pt

# LaTeX build products.
paper/*.aux
paper/*.log
paper/*.out
paper/*.bbl
paper/*.blg
paper/*.pdf

# local run logs
/runs_*.log

# Built manuscripts -- regenerate with: tectonic paper/audit.tex
paper/*.pdf
paper/*.log
paper/*.blg
paper/*.out

# Provenance is not data. The blanket /data/ rule above correctly keeps patient images and
# generated PNGs out of the repo, but it was also excluding the records that make any of
# this reproducible: which prompt produced which image, what it cost, what failed and why,
# and which images were in which split. Those are small text files we authored.
#
# Still excluded, deliberately: every image, and the face/identity embeddings. The identity
# analysis exists only to remove subject leakage from the splits; releasing its embeddings
# would hand out a face-matching index over a patient cohort, which is exactly what the
# ethics statement promises not to do.
!/data/synthetic/*/manifest.jsonl
!/data/synthetic/*/prompt_meta.json
!/data/splits_subject/*.jsonl
!/data/splits_subject/*.json
!/data/splits/*.jsonl
